check.check-content:
Step 1 Legacy.list format (per-line check) Run the following command to find uncommented deb / deb-src entries that lack a Signed-By option:
# grep -PRn -- '^\h*(deb(-src)?)\h+(\[(?![^\]]*\bSigned-By\b)[^\]]*\]|[^\[])'
\
/etc/apt/sources.list \
/etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.list 2>/dev/null
Nothing should be returned.
Note: This command checks each deb / deb-src line individually. It reports lines that either have no options bracket at all, or have an options bracket that does not include Signed-By. Commented lines ( #) are excluded.
Step 2 deb822.sources format (per-stanza check) Run the following script to find stanzas that have a URIs: field but no Signed-By: field:
#!/usr/bin/env bash
{
shopt -s nullglob
while IFS= read -r -d $'\0' l_file; do
awk '
BEGIN { uris=0; signed=0; lineno=0 }
/^[[:blank:]]*$/ {
if (uris && !signed)
print FILENAME ": stanza ending near line " lineno " is missing
Signed-By"
uris=0; signed=0
}
/^[[:blank:]]*URIs:[[:blank:]]*\S/ { uris=1 }
/^[[:blank:]]*Signed-By:[[:blank:]]*\S/ { signed=1 }
{ lineno=NR }
END { if (uris && !signed)
print FILENAME ": final stanza missing Signed-By" }
' "$l_file"
done < <(find /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ -maxdepth 1 -type f -name
'*.sources' -print0)
}
Nothing should be returned.

Run the following command and verify that the APT options for weak dependencies are disabled:
# /usr/bin/apt-config dump | /usr/bin/grep "APT::Install-"
Verify the output matches the following
APT::Install-Recommends "0";
APT::Install-Suggests "0";
Note: If no output is returned, this should be considered a failure as the default behavior is to install packages marked as recommended.

